<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI28-RSH-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI28-RSH-004" ;
  triage:title "Only transport call deadline-checked in drain(), not DB read" ;
  triage:description "The drain() function in peer_drain_coordinator.rs enforces a deadline (or timeout) for the network transport call when delivering messages to a peer, but does not enforce the same deadline on the prior database read that fetches the messages to deliver. Specifically, drain() now checks deadline.expired() immediately before and after the outbound.page_for_peer(...) call (lines 262-273), but page_for_peer itself takes no deadline/timeout parameter -- the DB read is bracketed by expiry checks, not actually bounded/interruptible. A slow or blocked SQLite read is not cancelled by the request deadline; only late-arriving results are rejected after the fact. Additionally, the OutboundMessageQuery::page_for_peer trait signature (contract.rs:663) lacks a deadline/budget parameter. This creates an asymmetry in deadline enforcement and reduces the reliability of the paging/delivery loop under database contention." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "Service-Hardening" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureEvidence "PR #659 (fix/ai27-28-cleanup-2 -> integrate/phase-AI, merge commit cbf2a66e). Re-verified against integrate/phase-AI current tip a6342ba9 (2026-07-26): OutboundMessageQuery::page_for_peer (crates/atm-storage/src/contract.rs:663) now takes a budget/deadline parameter; the rusqlite impl (crates/atm-storage-rusqlite/src/lib.rs:57) threads it into shared_db.rs, which sets connection.busy_timeout(budget) and installs a connection.progress_handler(1_000, || Instant::now() >= expires_at) so a slow/blocked SQLite read is genuinely interruptible, not just bracketed by after-the-fact expiry checks. drain() in peer_drain_coordinator.rs:281 passes its deadline straight through to page_for_peer. Dedicated test page_for_peer_rejects_an_expired_budget_before_opening_a_reader (lib.rs:785) covers the pre-expired case." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S8 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-07-25T16:53:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI28-RSH-004/pAI-s28/b7d8488/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI28-RSH-004/pAI-s28/b7d8488/2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

